<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Fairfax half year net profit falls.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Fairfax half year net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Dec 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    62.70 vs 93.98</p>
<p>    Net				     46.95 vs 62.38</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     3.50 vs 3.50</p>
<p>NOTE: John Fairfax Holdings Ltd is a newspaper group and is about 15 percent owned by Kerry Packer's Publishing and Broadcasting Ltd and 19.9 percent owned by Brierley Investments Ltd which is seeking shareholder approval to move to 25 percent. </p>
<p>    Sales				  511.58 vs 514.41</p>
<p>    Other income			   3.92 vs 2.19</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    5.90 vs 7.84</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			  nil vs loss 0.92</p>
<p>Dividend is unfranked</p>
<p>Pay date Apr 30</p>
<p>Reg date Apr 16</p>
<p>    Tax				     15.73 vs 31.56</p>
<p>    Interest				35.42 vs 20.27</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  31.82 vs 19.68</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.01 vs 0.04</p>
</text>
